+# v17.09-shared — follow-up B: hourly best-of index is rebuilt only when something it uses changed
+
+Part of the CPU work (v17.07). Separate change; not part of the first 48-hour Orlando pilot.
+
+## What the index depends on (traced)
+`computeBestIndex` reads only `businesses` rows: existence, `cs`, `sub`, `hood`, `rat`, `rev` (the filter
+`rat>=4 AND rev>=5 AND sub<>''`, grouped by cs/sub/hood). Hidden listings (duplicate, out-of-area, competitor,
+removed by the sync or an admin) are DELETEd from `businesses`; there is no separate visibility flag. Write paths
+found: sync upsert and stale/competitor/out-of-area deletes, insertOne/refreshOne (claims, approvals, owner edits,
+payments, listing verification), dedupe, merges (re-point/delete), admin delete/edit routes, the sub-category
+re-map in migrate. Rather than add tracking to each, D1 itself counts changes:
+
+## Change
+- migrate creates `meta.best_gen` and three triggers on `businesses` (idempotent `IF NOT EXISTS`, inside try/catch):
+  after INSERT, after DELETE, and after UPDATE OF rat/rev/sub/cs/hood **only when a value really changed**
+  (`OLD.x IS NOT NEW.x`). Each bumps `best_gen`. Covers every current and future code path.
+- `computeBestIndex(DB, true)` (hourly cron only) reads best_gen first, and skips when the stored index was built at
+  the same best_gen, by the same code version (BUILD), less than 24 h ago. Rebuilds when the index or the counter is
+  missing, the version changed, a day passed, or anything changed. The index and its build stamp are written together.
+- A change made during a rebuild leaves best_gen ahead of the stored stamp → rebuilt next hour. A failed rebuild
+  writes nothing → the last good index keeps being served → retried next hour. bestIndex() and other callers unchanged.
+
+## Expected saving — small
+Orlando's index query groups 2,865 rows (13,588 rows read on D1) once an hour; the Worker-side part is the JSON
+work on those rows, a few ms per run → well under 1% of the scheduled CPU. The D1 reads (~326k rows/day) are saved
+too. The cost is three triggers on the main table (each a one-row meta update when a listing really changes).
+Recommendation: ship only if the D1 reads matter; the CPU gain alone is marginal.
+
+## Tests (scripts/qa/cron-cpu.test.mjs)
+26/26: first build; unchanged → skip; phone edit → skip; same value rewritten → skip; rating, sub-category,
+neighbourhood, category, review count → rebuild; delete → rebuild and correct count; new listing via sync →
+rebuild; merge re-point (same data) → skip; failed rebuild keeps the last good index and retries; edit during a
+rebuild stays pending and is included next run; missing index / other version / >1 day / no counter → rebuild;
+migrate repeatable (3 triggers). Local suite 99/99 (triggers created by migrate in the local D1).
+
+## Status
+- Committed on branch cpu-followups; not deployed.
